You problem appears to be that you are not the same person who compiled
the nethack binary.  The nethack binary is compiled with the set user-id
bit turned on, allowing all users to assume the user-id of the nethack
binary while playing.  In order to prevent nethack abuse, the directory
in the playground where games are saved is only writeable by the user-id
of nethack.  

When you compiled recover, if you are not the same user-id as nethack,
you can't write to the save directory, hence no recover is possible.

Sounds like you need to get the sysadmin to make and install recover
for you, and to straighten out the permissions.

